  "notes": "Mimetic word for speaking indistinctly with the mouth barely opening, typically from hesitation or embarrassment. Also describes slow movement inside a closed mouth.\n\nUSAGE:\n- As adverb: もごもご{話|はな}す (to mumble)\n- With する: もごもごする (to mumble; to fidget with the mouth)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ぼそぼそ: muttering — low, quiet, flat murmuring\n- もぐもぐ: munching; mumbling — emphasizes chewing/mouth movement",
